course: dictionary
lesson: 12655
title: Disreputable: not to be trusted
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Some words warn you about people, places and things. Disreputable is one of them. It means the person or place is known for being dishonest or doing bad things, so people do not trust them. «The old inn had a disreputable owner who cheated his guests.» The guests were cheated, so the owner cannot be trusted. Disreputable means not to be trusted.
explain: The word can also describe how something looks. «The disreputable-looking man had torn clothes and muddy boots.» Torn clothes and muddy boots make him look dirty and shabby, not respectable. Looking disreputable does not always mean being bad, but it does give people a reason to be careful.
explain: Read the words around the word to find its meaning. Ask yourself: what does this sentence say about the person, place or thing? Then swap in your meaning: «The inn had a dishonest owner who cheated his guests» still makes sense, so you are right.
fact: Disreputable is an adjective. You can say a disreputable trader, or a disreputable company.
fact: «Disreputable» means known for being dishonest or doing bad things, so people do not trust or respect you.
fact: «Disreputable» can also mean looking dirty, shabby or not respectable.
fact: «A disreputable website» may cheat you, so be careful before you share your password or money.
fact: The opposite of disreputable is respectable: a respectable shop is one people trust.
exercise: «The old inn had a disreputable owner who cheated his guests.» What does disreputable mean here? | Very rich and kind to guests | Brand new and very clean | *Known for being dishonest, so people do not trust him | Full of music and dancing
exercise: Ella says a website that asks for your password might be disreputable. What does that suggest? | It is slow to load | It is the best website in the world | It is a website all about cats | *It may cheat you, so be careful
exercise: «The disreputable-looking man had torn clothes and muddy boots.» What do the torn clothes and muddy boots suggest about the man? | *He looked shabby and not respectable | He had just won a race | He was very tall | He was a famous king
test: «Grandad said the disreputable trader sold fake watches.» What is a disreputable trader? | *A seller who cannot be trusted | A trader who sells only fruit at the market | A kind teacher who gives out prizes | A seller who gives free gifts
test: Which word is closest in meaning to disreputable? | Tiny | Famous | *Dishonest | Cheerful
exam: Why should you be careful with a disreputable website? | Because it is quick and bright | Because it sells books about history | Because it is written in another language | *Because it may cheat you
